Maintaining an accurate inventory of Azure resources helps administrators understand their environment, control costs, and simplify governance activities.

An inventory should include:

* Resource names
* Resource types
* Subscription details
* Resource groups
* Owners
* Business purpose
* Environment classification
* Lifecycle status

# Real-Life Example:
For example, administrators can quickly identify unused virtual machines that are no longer associated with active business projects.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is organizations performing annual infrastructure reviews to eliminate obsolete cloud resources.

Accurate resource inventories improve operational visibility and governance.
